      "notes": "Unchanged from the references: the dark bezel around a single green CRT screen (#08120c fill, #2f6b3f hairline frame, #8ee39a ink, #c9ffd4 highlights, amber readout and red/blue/green/amber ID tones), the Status strip across the top, narrow left rail of small key/value blocks, big round scope centre-left, stacked tables on the right, one wide control row and the F1\\u2013F12 key strip with its brass plate along the bottom. From the profile came the eight track columns in order (TRK/SPD/ALT/TYPE/ID/FIRE/TTI/PK), the four identification states with their tones, the 120\\u00b0 fixed-sector and per-class detection figures, the 70/50/20 km bands and the two-rockets-in-air limit shown as a readout, plus a decision row sized for the seven-step commit sequence. This revision keeps the earlier press-and-drag panning on the scope slot and now anchors the radar port so running interception messages cannot shrink it: the side columns are fixed pixel widths (rail 112px, tracks 300px, resources 216px), the main grid row is minmax(0,1fr), every panel body is overflow:hidden with its injected slot scrolling internally, and the decision slot has a fixed 78px height instead of a min-height \\u2014 so the scope simply absorbs all remaining pixels. I also trimmed header/footer padding, the scope footer legend and rail label widths to give the scope more area. The F-key strip and the ID/fire keys are fixed lamps and labels, not pressable controls; the only real controls are the range and decision slots.",
